Source: zerosdr
Section: hamradio
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Weiming Feng <bestedwin@gmail.com>
Build-Depends: debhelper (>= 10), cmake, librtlsdr-dev, libasound2-dev, libpulse-dev, libfreetype-dev, libc6-dev, nlohmann-json3-dev
Standards-Version: 4.1.3

Package: zerosdr
Architecture: arm64
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, libasound2-plugins, curl
Description: Pocket SDR receiver for Cardputer Zero and Linux handhelds
 A graphical SDR application optimized for small SPI displays.
 Supports RTL-SDR devices with spectrum and waterfall, FM/NFM/AM/USB/LSB
 audio, ADSB aircraft, AIS vessels, ACARS messages, APRS stations and an
 RFI survey.
 .
 Features:
  - Real-time spectrum and waterfall with SDR memories
  - FM/NFM/AM/USB/LSB demodulation with squelch and audio AGC
  - ADSB radar, aircraft list and PFD detail view
  - AIS vessels with map/CPA and NMEA UDP output
  - ACARS messages and APRS station tracking
  - Wideband spectrum and RFI survey pages
  - Optimized for Raspberry Pi Zero 2W / Pi 5 and M5Stack Cardputer Zero
